Thanks for reviewing!

Because `is_user_mode` is protected by 4-byte PMP region in `z_riscv_init_user_accesses()`, `is_user_mode` will be 8-byte and be larger than PMP region in RV64.
```
struct riscv_pmp_region dynamic_regions[] = {
  {
    /* MCU state */
    .start = (ulong_t) &is_user_mode,
    .size = 4,
    .perm = PMP_R,
    .mode = PMP_MODE_NA4,
  }, ...

// p.s. Origin RISC-V PMP code will use 4-byte PMP region for it, I haven't change it in my PMP patch.
```

`is_user_mode` only needs 1-byte so I don't enlarge PMP region but shrink size of `is_user_mode`  in RV64.
